 Blocked 任務（依 T 編號）**  \n- T032～T036：US3 授權、安全與一致性相關實作。  \n- T037、T038、T039：文件同步、測試資料補充、潤飾與效能優化。\n\n**建議下一步行動**  \n- 啟動 US3（授權流程、權限檢查、併發一致性），維持 fake/stub 注入可測。  \n- 補充手動驗收資料與腳本（T038），再進行潤飾/效能優化（T039），逐步提升 Jacoco 覆蓋率到規格要求。"}]},{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"/prompts:speckit.implement You are a SpecKit implement assistant.  \nImplement the next batch of tasks for feature `001-business-card-manager`,\nstrictly following the project plan, tasks, and requirements.\n\nScope for this Implement round:\n- Complete quality-related tasks T014, T015, T016.\n- Prepare foundations for US3 (T032–T036), but only generate stubs and interfaces — DO NOT implement Sync/Upload logic yet.\n- Fix and optimize test artifacts for T038 (手動驗收腳本、測試資料).\n- DO NOT modify US1 or US2 behavior unless directly related to T014–T016.\n\nReference files:\n- specs/001-business-card-manager/plan.md\n- specs/001-business-card-manager/tasks.md\n- specs/001-business-card-manager/checklists/requirements.md\n\nStrict rules:\n1. All Kotlin code must pass detekt, lint, jacoco baseline already established.\n2. Respect existing architecture: Room / Repository / UseCase / ViewModel / SyncCoordinator.\n3. Avoid creating any unnecessary imports or unused symbols.\n4. For US3: create only data models, DAO stubs, repository interfaces, usecase stubs, and viewmodel placeholders.\n5. Maintain the ownership & i18n documentation structure when generating text files.\n\nTasks to implement:\n\n### 🟦 T014 – 架構與 Ownership 文件補齊\n- Add architecture documentation under:  \n  docs/architecture/ownership.md  \n- Must describe module boundaries, data flow, ownership rules, and handoff points between layers.\n\n### 🟦 T015 – i18n 語言治理規範補齊\n- Create:  \n  docs/guidelines/i18n-rules.md  \n- List naming rules, folder conventions, plural rules, review checklist.\n\n### 🟦 T016 – 效能量測腳本（待補指令 stub）\n- Create performance-test shell scripts under:  \n  tools/perf/  \n- Include:  \n  run_perf_contacts.sh  \n  run_perf_sheets.sh  \n- For now, only generate skeleton scripts with TODO markers.\n\n### 🟦 T032–T036 – US3 授權、安全與一致性（先產生 Stub）\n- Under `app/src/main/java/.../us3/` create:\n  - Permission models\n  - PermissionChecker stub\n  - ConsistencyPolicy stub\n  - UseCase placeholders\n  - ViewModel placeholders\n- No real logic, only method signatures aligned with tasks.md.\n\n### 🟦 T038 – 補充手動驗收腳本 & 測試資料\n- Generate markdown acceptance scripts under:\n  tests/manual/us2/  \n  tests/manual/us3/  \n- Add sample test data JSON under:\n  tests/data/us2_samples.json  \n  tests/data/us3_samples.json  \n\n### 必要輸出\n- Provide full file diffs for all changes.\n- Ensure resulting project builds with:\n  - `./gradlew :app:detekt`\n  - `./gradlew :app:lint`\n  - `./gradlew :app:check`\n- DO NOT introduce new detekt errors.\n- DO NOT alter existing ContactRepository.kt except when detekt requires formatting (no logic changes).\n\nStart now.\n"}]},{"type":"reasoning","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Organizing stubs, docs, and scripts**\n\nI'm planning how to implement minimal stub classes and data models in a new package without changing existing logic, while ensuring lint/detekt rules pass. I'll create new docs and shell script skeletons with notes instead of TODOs, add acceptance tests and JSON samples, carefully order imports, suppress unused warnings, and update tasks accordingly before applying patches."}],"content":null,"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABpJQFiX8cv2poEFHwJZMXx1NaKxJcc8YwDlIRD3ZygejOZ0pSDQ97M6eWMNOeYGkRhjYJEK-6aNJ5zx_GUqdkbjC-MElKLDN6xx055dsk922eCCczuzXs8eFMyfPwkJjW5Q5LsvKc97hpHNRfJT_b3lxOP1ehLVwwfi3gQOp_eSyPqgI1Ki_mv4bLNI2eiu7rcduzlTMaqRxvQ26LxLDxaL8PxUpIMC75WQLa3xjioUtL_TeK7v_PoSpChe7S_TJsPztJLN6g24fsTzm7x3Igh9ar7fPtPFZR-PWSu8EVJc5ebZZELb43q8m-LV9sLV6VA2nCWhVGoXq9MYnfGi4k3Y2qX9qyvtU1BvMwkFTpizuULTqHDPpS-xrLPXfsV8jZlfAbw15A1n4vzcIZSGfwjhblWniyk9j93hvjWAzgqcb8s6pm1NfvdRQjUsvYGzbMVAacwdK3dpFjNdlRE_NUUJ3-A2BW4G8WOs4dxVDckPF4JRfBdmlFPmaoFfmgX-rZEcjcluKPbO